# Enfusion AI (living)

Part of the engine handbook `.cursor/rules/enfusion-enforce.mdc`; the same rules for adding facts apply (one bullet: claim, consequence, evidence; changelog line in the handbook).

## AI / behavior trees

- **Native group despawn and the common entity helper use the same per-entity teardown.** `SCR_AIGroup.DespawnMembers()` loops through controlled characters calling `RplComponent.DeleteRplEntity(entity, false)`; `SCR_EntityHelper.DeleteEntityAndChildren()` is a one-line wrapper around that call. Changing helper names is not evidence of faster removal. Bound work between transactions and measure character costs; stock interior cleanup's 30-prop cap is not a safe-character benchmark. Evidence: `Game/Entities/SCR_AIGroup.c:2864-2906`; `Game/Helpers/SCR_EntityHelper.c:174-180`; `Game/Destruction/SCR_RegionalDestructionManager.c:211-256` (source inspection).
- **GM editor AI budget is separate from a mission's logical roster.** Editable-character removal unregisters it through `SCR_EditableEntityCore`, which queues negative budget changes; group prefab costs can also exist independently. Keeping an addon roster or group is not by itself evidence that an unchanged character AI budget is correct. Verify physical entity removal and editor accounting separately. Evidence: `Game/Editor/Components/EditableEntity/SCR_EditableEntityComponent.c:2190-2215`; `Game/Editor/Core/SCR_EditableEntityCore.c:148-150,886-940`; `SCR_EditableGroupComponent.c:433-496` (source inspection).
- **`SCR_AIGroup.AddAIEntityToGroup` success does not prove membership in that group.** It activates the control agent, adds it only if `GetParentGroup()` is null, then returns true even when the agent already belongs to another group. Validate the resulting parent before counting a restored soldier as attached; preserve player ownership when repairing affiliation. Evidence: `Game/Entities/SCR_AIGroup.c:1920-1937` (source inspection).
- **Group dormancy is not a per-soldier state snapshot.** In the local GameSources revision, `SCR_AIGroup.DespawnMembers()` retains aggregate alive/dead counts and deletes member entities; `SpawnMembers()` rebuilds prefab slots using group formation placement. Scenario Framework `SlotAI.DynamicDespawn()` also stores one `m_vPosition`, and `InitGroupComponents()` reforms agents around it. Exact individual positions, casualty identities, loadouts and combat state require a separate verified snapshot/restore path; do not infer that fidelity from the dynamic-spawn API names. Evidence: `Game/Entities/SCR_AIGroup.c:1657-1757,2777-2792,2864-2906`; `Game/ScenarioFramework/Components/SCR_ScenarioFrameworkSlotAI.c:91-126,323-362` (source inspection, not a live round-trip test).
- **Native group dormancy still notifies empty-group listeners.** `SCR_AIGroup.OnEmpty()` invokes `Event_OnEmpty` before checking `IsDormant()`. Consumers must distinguish intentional virtualization from elimination before deleting members; the native dormant guard only prevents the later automatic group-entity deletion. Evidence: `Game/Entities/SCR_AIGroup.c:2442-2454` (source inspection).
- **Group member notifications invoke script listeners inline.** `OnAgentAdded` / `OnAgentRemoved` call their invokers directly. Hold managed transaction records in local `ref`s across membership changes, recheck owner/roster afterward, and latch cleanup state before callback-producing deletion. Evidence: `Game/Entities/SCR_AIGroup.c:2458-2475` (source inspection; not a reproduced live retirement crash).
- **Defend waypoint fast init teleports soldiers to smart actions or turret seats.** Call `SCR_DefendWaypoint.SetFastInit(false)` for garrisons that must walk into position. `SCR_AIAllocateActionsForDefendActivity` reads `GetFastInit()` and passes it to `OccupySA` / `OccupyTurret`; false still reserves and messages the action so native movement handles entry. Evidence: `Game/AI/Group/SCR_DefendWaypoint.c`; `Game/AI/ScriptedNodes/Groups/SCR_AIAllocateActionsForDefendActivity.c:67,135-165`.
- **Waypoint priority level is added to soldier behavior priority, not just waypoint selection.** `SCR_AIDefendActivity.SendDefendSector` forwards it to `SCR_AIDefendBehavior`: level 20 makes Defend score 61+20=81, beating ordinary attack initiation (70) and `SCR_AIObserveThreatSystemBehavior`'s high-priority gunfire response (69). Use normal level 0 for autonomous garrisons; rare high-threat attacks can otherwise mask the starvation. Evidence: `Game/AI/Behavior/SCR_AIDefendActivity.c`, `SCR_AIAttackBehavior.c`, `SCR_AIObserveThreatSystemBehavior.c`; native `Evaluate()` regression `IA_BaseGarrisonTest` logged 81/61/70/69 (2026-09-05).
- **`PerceptionManager` is separate from `SCR_AIWorld`.** The vanilla `SCR_AIWorld.et` / `SCR_AIWorld_Eden.et` and `GameMode_Base.et` do not include it. Check the world's full inheritance before assuming an AI world supplies perception. `SCR_AIDangerReaction_WeaponFired.NotifyGroup` silently returns when `GetGame().GetPerceptionManager()` is null; the AIScript "Show perception panel" displays `PerceptionManager not found!`. Evidence: `Prefabs/World/Game/PerceptionManager.et`; `Game/AI/Reaction/Danger/SCR_AIDangerReaction_WeaponFired.c:140-144`; `Game/AI/SCR_AIDebugVisualization.c:180-183`. A missing manager in local layers is a diagnostic lead, not runtime proof that an inherited world lacks one.
- **Vanilla `AIWaypoint_Patrol` is one Move, not a looping route.** Prefab uses `WP_Patrol.bt` with `CompletionRadius 5` / `CompletionType Any`. The group walks to that point and the waypoint completes; it will idle unless a new WP is issued. Chain Moves (or re-issue on empty) for a patrol. Evidence: `Prefabs/AI/Waypoints/AIWaypoint_Patrol.et`; `runtime:` elite patrols stood still after the single jittered Patrol WP completed.
- **`Group.bt` only re-runs `SCR_AIDecideActivity` every 0.3s.** Typed waypoint trees re-read `GetCurrentWaypoint()` with no `WaypointIn` and `NodeError` unless the class matches: `ActivityDefend.bt` needs `SCR_DefendWaypoint`, `GetInNearestVehicle.bt` (from `ActivityGetIn.bt`) needs `SCR_BoardingTimedWaypoint`. Same-frame `RemoveAllOrders` + Move/S&D/GetOut leaves the old tree running. Leave current null until the next DecideActivity, or wait ~400 ms. GetInNearest is `Autocomplete 0`, so it stays current until removed. Evidence: `Group.bt` Idle Period 0.3; `SCR_AIGetDefendWaypointParameters.c:21`; `SCR_AIGetInNearestWaypointParameters.c:20`; `runtime:` `Wrong class of provided Waypoint!`
- **`SCR_AIFindAvailableVehicle.HasNoAvailableCompartment` NPEs if boarding params were GC'd.** It reads `m_WaypointParameter.m_bIsDriverAllowed` with no null check. That member is not a `ref`; `GetAllowance()` lives on the waypoint. Removing GetInNearest (Autocomplete 0) while the tree still ticks nulls the pointer. The sphere-query path comments "waypoint can be deleted in the meantime"; the cached-vehicle path still calls the callback. Fail the search when params are missing. Evidence: `SCR_AIFindAvailableVehicle.c:66-104`; `runtime:` `NULL pointer … m_bIsDriverAllowed`.
- **`PreventMaxLOD` is visible as `GetPermanentLOD() != -1`.** Vanilla group diagnostics treat that as “this agent must stay simulated.” Addon cache/eviction that refuses any forced LOD will also refuse soldiers the addon itself pinned for inbound walking. Ignore only an arrival-owned pin, or `AllowMaxLOD` before snapshot. Evidence: `Game/generated/AI/AIAgent.c` GetPermanentLOD/PreventMaxLOD; `SCR_AIGroup.c:2811`; `runtime:` hold/cover groups remaining fully spawned while ordinary patrols cached.
- **`SCR_AIToggleMaxLOD` OnAbort NodeErrors if `AgentIn` was never written.** `HandleFailedNavlinkDoor.bt` (from `MoveToLocation.bt`) keeps a Parallel sibling with `m_bPerformOnAbort 1` that AllowMaxLODs on abort. `GetVariableIn` is false until `SCR_AISelectDoorOperatorAgent` writes `agent`; aborting the move first is `No agent provided!`. Vanilla already treats a written-null agent as SUCCESS. Evidence: `SCR_AIToggleMaxLOD.c:31-48`; `HandleFailedNavlinkDoor.bt`; `runtime:` MoveToLocation / HandleFailedNavlinkDoor OnAbort.
- **`SCR_AIGetSuppressionVolumeCenterPosition` NodeErrors if the volume was GC'd.** `SuppressBehavior.bt` Parallel keeps ticking after `SCR_AISuppressGroupClusterBehavior` Completes/Fails (cluster dropped, members inside the scaled box, `SetGroupSuppressClusterState` swap). The volume is a `ref` on the action, so the blackboard object goes null. Sibling `SCR_AIUpdateTargetSuppressionData` already FAILs; this node and `SCR_AIGetSuppressionVolumeLine` call `NodeError` / `Debug.Error`. Evidence: `SCR_AIGetSuppressionVolumePosition.c:24-25` / `:73-74`; `SCR_AIUpdateTargetSuppressionData.c:46-47`; `runtime:` Enhanced Defense `No suppression volume provided!`.
- **`SCR_AIProcessFailedMovementResult` NPEs if the group has no leader, and NodeErrors on UNKNOWN waypoint-related fails.** `MoveToLocation.bt` calls it after Group Move fails; line 59 does `m_Group.GetLeaderEntity().GetOrigin()` with only `m_Group` checked (`#return` on wipe / staggered spawn / empty slot). `EMoveError.UNKNOWN` is "configuration error - missing component, navmesh etc."; vanilla then `NodeErrorOnce` and returns RUNNING so the group stays stuck for debug (`:97-101`). Complete the waypoint and fail the action instead. Evidence: `SCR_AIProcessFailedMovementResult.c:59` / `:97-101`; `EMoveError.c`; `runtime:` `#return` after infantry spawn; `runtime:` Failed move St Pierre Radio Tower after objective spawn.
- **Vanilla never releases a group's smart-action allocation.** The Defend search (`SCR_AIFindSmartActions`) hands every post it finds to `AllocateSmartActions`, which appends it to the group's list and sets it inaccessible. `ReleaseSmartActions` restores accessibility and clears the list; `ReleaseSmartAction` only removes one entry. Neither has a vanilla script caller. A soldier's `ReleaseAction` (action end, failure or death) makes that one post accessible again but leaves it in the list. `SCR_AIAllocateActionsForDefendActivity` fills posts from the front of the whole accumulated list, so a group whose Defend area moved can walk back to old posts, and posts it never used stay locked. Call `ReleaseSmartActions()` before re-tasking a Defend group. To free another group's idle post, `ReleaseSmartAction` it, then `SetActionAccessible(true)`. `GetAllocatedSmartActions` returns the live list, so iterate a copy. Evidence: `Game/Entities/SCR_AIGroup.c:1986-2068`; `SCR_AIFindSmartActions.c:45-49`; `SCR_AIAllocateActionsForDefendActivity.c:85-107`; `SCR_AISmartActionComponent.c:18-40`.
- **Script-moving a Defend waypoint does not restart the group's cover search for up to 180 s.** `ActivityDefend.bt` re-runs the search when `SCR_AIOnWaypointPropertiesChange` succeeds, or after its 150 s + 0–30 s timeout. That node listens only to the waypoint's `GetOnWaypointPropertiesChanged()` invoker. `SCR_AIWaypoint.OnTransformResetImpl` fires it, and the GM editor calls `OnTransformReset()` after a move, but `SetOrigin` + `Update()` does not (`OnTransformReset` is the caller's job after a transform discontinuity). After a script move, call `OnTransformReset()` or invoke the event, as vanilla `SCR_AISetDefendWaypointParameters` does after a preset change. Evidence: `data/AI/BehaviorTrees/Chimera/Group/ActivityDefend.bt:139-144`; `SCR_AIOnWaypointPropertiesChange.c:44-72`; `SCR_AIWaypoint.c:49-54`; `SCR_EditableEntityComponent.c:760`; `GameLib/generated/Entities/GenericEntity.c:85-99`; `SCR_AISetDefendWaypointParameters.c:70`. Source reading; not yet runtime-proven.
- **Group perception ignores aircraft; soldiers still shoot at them.** `SCR_AIGroupPerception` skips `EAIUnitType.UnitType_Aircraft` perceivables ("no reason to track aircrafts in group perception"), so a group never tracks or suppresses a helicopter as a group. Soldier target selection still scores aircraft at 90.0 / −0.015 (infantry 100.0 / −0.1). A group-level air-raid response must be scripted. Evidence: `Game/AI/Group/SCR_AIGroupPerception.c:214-217, 272-275, 298-301`; `Game/AI/Components/SCR_AICombatComponent.c:1214-1218`.
